{
  "dom_id": "step-q333814",
  "name": "Question 9",
  "problem": "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{\u2032}(t)=x(t)+y(t) \\\\ {y}^{\u2032}(t)=3x(t)+3y(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear differential equations above. The eigenvalues of the system's matrix are ${\\lambda }_{1}=0$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=4,$ for which the corresponding eigenvectors are ${v}_{1}=[-1,\\text{\u00a0}1]^{T}$ and ${v}_{2}=[1,\\text{\u00a0}3]^{T},$ respectively. Which of the following could represent the phase portrait of the system?\n\n*Hint: Here, the dotted line represents the equilibrium solutions.*",
  "worked_solution": "The general solution of the system is\n\n$$\nx(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}]={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}{e}^{4t}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nLet's now sketch the phase portrait.\n\n- First, notice that ${x}_{E}(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ are the equilibrium solutions of the system since ${x}_{E}^{\u2032}(t)=0.$ These solutions form the line with the equation $y=-x$ in the phase space, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069892/assets/bdfe2e3f89db20665d2c7c1e49c7ddae42387fc1e5bdde8849a9ed1de7e33687.png)\n\n- Now, the line that passes through the origin and is parallel to ${v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]$ has the equation \n$y=3x$\nand the straight-line solutions of the form\n${c}_{2}{e}^{4t}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]$\nlie on that line. Since ${e}^{4t}\\to \\infty $ as $t\\to \\infty ,$ these solutions approach infinity as $t\\to \\infty .$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069892/assets/99629c2f73e3a10db2ef139848c93c6a2489d995d3d992b7dfb0332989b4f48f.png)\n\nAll other non-equilibrium solutions are parallel to the vector ${v}_{2}.$ So, the phase portrait of our system looks as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069892/assets/cb491075c2fecf4aa28f4b167e91ac5a0b7475cf57c1b43eb94e8e1427a28922.png)",
